# Fragment for Fedora's own realtime flavour (rpmbuild --with realtime --with rtonly,
# kernel-x86_64-rt-fedora.config in kernel-7.2.11-200.fc44). Installed by
# scripts/lab/build-rt-kernel.sh as SOURCES/kernel-local, which kernel.spec
# (Source3001) merges into every flavour's config.
#
# Fedora's rt config already sets everything an RT kernel needs, checked against
# the v7.2.11 Kconfig: CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT=y (needs EXPERT && ARCH_SUPPORTS_RT),
# CONFIG_PREEMPT=y with PREEMPT_LAZY off (NONE/VOLUNTARY depend on !PREEMPT_RT),
# NO_HZ_FULL, RCU_NOCB_CPU, RCU_BOOST, RCU_NOCB_CPU_CB_BOOST, HZ_1000 and
# HIGH_RES_TIMERS. Nothing is repeated here.
#
# The one setting missing for a latency kernel: the rt flavour has
# CONFIG_DEBUG_PREEMPT=y (kernel/Kconfig.debug: depends on PREEMPTION &&
# DEBUG_KERNEL), which instruments smp_processor_id() and preempt-count checks
# on hot paths. The stock Fedora kernel leaves it off; do the same here.
# CONFIG_DEBUG_PREEMPT is not set
